        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="material, obsolete" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The dataset can be applied to describe an average entrance door of a one-family house. The door frame is made of steel (paint coated), the door leaf is made of wood, planked with powder coated aluminium on both sides. The lock, door handles and frame joints are fabricated from steel. Data are based on a door of 0.8x2.0 m and scaled to 1m2. 1 m2 of the aluminium planked massive wood outer door weighs 38.8 kg. The functional life time for the door frame is 60 years, for the door leaf it is 30 years. Wood input linked to updated supply chain based on information obtained from Frank Werner. Philippe Stolz, August 2016.\nGeography: Data from producers in Switzerland.\nTechnology: The technology represents average European production.\nVersion: 2.2\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Türen\nUVEK 2022 source file:07151.XML\n\n&#10;UUID: 7c9ca4c8-8b61-3a61-be06-b04285f98d3b" includedProcesses="This dataset describes the production of 1m2 (visible area) outer door, (entrance door), including the processes for the installation. Not included are transports from plant to construction site. " infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="material, obsolete" localName="xxx Door, outer, wood-aluminium, at plant" localSubCategory="construction, obsolete\doors, obsolete" name="xxx Door, outer, wood-aluminium, at plant" subCategory="construction, obsolete\doors, obsolete" unit="m2"/>
